IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfac-239`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2) -- Prospectus requirements: s 240. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is "the TEXT says no in its own words"; NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every "no" branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`, every "not covered" branch `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- Periods are counted by sfa-periods.l4 (conventions P1 to P10 of the keel's NOTES.md): "within N days after X" opens the day after X (P2).
-- The Act's "such requirements as the Authority may prescribe" and "such period as the Authority may prescribe" are INPUTS (a fact, or a number of days).

-- inert (reason 1), lines 38374-38378: Subdivision (2) heading and the marginal heading of s 240: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 38379-38379: s 240(1) opening words: each limb is encoded in the function that follows.
-- repealed or blank in this text, lines 38547-38547: s 240(6): "[Deleted by Act 1 of 2005]".
-- inert (reason 2), lines 38606-38610: s 240(8B): the Authority may prescribe the same or different periods and days for different offers; a rule-making power, the period it prescribes is an input of s 240(8) and s 240(8A).
-- inert (reason 2), lines 38823-38826: s 240(20): regulations made under this section may make a contravention an offence with penalties up to a fine of $50,000; a regulation-making power.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 38827-38827: s 240AA marginal heading: not operative.

§ `s 240(1): the requirement for a prospectus`

DECLARE `s 240(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 240(1) make the offer`

-- s 240(1): the bar. "unless the offer" is a closed gate; "A person must not make an offer" is the element the bar is limited to.
-- src:38379 | 240.—(1) A person must not make an offer of securities or
-- src:38380 | securities‑based derivatives contracts unless the offer —
-- src:38382 | (a) is made in or accompanied by a prospectus in respect of the
-- src:38383 | offer —
-- src:38385 | (i) that is prepared in accordance with section 243;
-- src:38387 | (ii) a copy of which, being one that has been signed in
-- src:38388 | accordance with subsection (4A), is lodged with the
-- src:38389 | Authority; and
-- src:38391 | (iii) that is registered by the Authority; and
-- src:38396 | (b) complies with such requirements as the Authority may
-- src:38397 | prescribe.
@ref s 240(1) (src:38379-38397)
GIVEN
    `the person makes an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts (as section 239(6) says when a person makes an offer)?
    `this Subdivision applies to the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239A(1) and (2), s 239(8) and Subdivision (4): this Subdivision applies to the offer` answer for the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus in respect of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made in, or accompanied by, a prospectus in respect of the offer?
    `the prospectus is prepared in accordance with section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus prepared in accordance with section 243 (the contents section)?
    `a copy of the prospectus signed in accordance with section 240(4A) is lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy of the prospectus, signed as section 240(4A) requires, lodged with the Authority?
    `the prospectus is registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered the prospectus?
    `the offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer comply with the requirements the Authority has prescribed for the purpose of section 240(1)(b)?
    `the offer is made in or accompanied by a profile statement in accordance with section 240(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240(4) the offer may be made in or accompanied by a profile statement instead of a prospectus` answer for the offer? (JUST TRUE if the route is open; any other answer is read as the route not being shown open.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F4 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240(1) the person must not make the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person makes an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus in respect of the offer` AND `the prospectus is prepared in accordance with section 243` AND `a copy of the prospectus signed in accordance with section 240(4A) is lodged with the Authority` AND `the prospectus is registered by the Authority` AND `the offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the offer (a) is made in or accompanied by a prospectus in respect of the offer (i) that is prepared in accordance with section 243; (ii) a copy of which, being one that has been signed in accordance with subsection (4A), is lodged with the Authority; and (iii) that is registered by the Authority; and (b) complies with such requirements as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the offer is made in or accompanied by a profile statement in accordance with section 240(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite subsection (1), an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts may be made in or accompanied by an extract from, or an abridged version of, a prospectus (called in this section a profile statement), instead of a prospectus"
        IF `this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to an offer of securities"
        IF `this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer of another provision (the disapplication of this Subdivision) was not worked out
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 240(1) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:38379-38397)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is the person who makes the offer?
    `what section 240(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240(1) the person must not make the offer` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 240(1) action`
`s 240(1) the person shall not make the offer without a registered prospectus` MEANS
    IF `what section 240(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 240(1) make the offer`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the offer was made without the prospectus section 240(1) requires; section 240(7) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 240(2): lodging a preliminary document is lodging a prospectus.
-- src:38401 | (2) A person who lodges a preliminary document with the
-- src:38402 | Authority is deemed to have lodged a prospectus with the Authority.
@ref s 240(2) (src:38401-38402)
GIVEN
    `the person lodges a preliminary document with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person lodge a preliminary document with the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(2) the person is deemed to have lodged a prospectus with the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the person lodges a preliminary document with the Authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the deeming reaches the person who lodges a preliminary document and says nothing of another person

-- s 240(3): a preliminary document must contain all the information a prospectus must contain, but for what the Authority prescribes.
-- src:38404 | (3) A preliminary document referred to in subsection (2) must
-- src:38405 | contain all information to be included in a prospectus other than such
-- src:38406 | information as the Authority may prescribe.
@ref s 240(3) (src:38404-38406)
GIVEN
    `the document is a preliminary document referred to in section 240(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a preliminary document that the person has lodged with the Authority (section 240(2))?
    `the document contains all the information to be included in a prospectus other than such information as the Authority may prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document contain all the information that a prospectus must contain, other than information the Authority has prescribed may be left out?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(3) the preliminary document contains all the information it must contain` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the document is a preliminary document referred to in section 240(2)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A preliminary document referred to in subsection (2) must contain all information to be included in a prospectus"
        IF `the document contains all the information to be included in a prospectus other than such information as the Authority may prescribe`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain all information to be included in a prospectus other than such information as the Authority may prescribe"

-- s 240(4): the profile statement route. Named for a permission ("may be made") whose "if" gate failed: NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1); fork F5).
-- src:38408 | (4) Despite subsection (1), an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:38409 | derivatives contracts may be made in or accompanied by an extract
-- src:38410 | from, or an abridged version of, a prospectus (called in this section a
-- src:38411 | profile statement), instead of a prospectus, if —
-- src:38413 | (a) a prospectus in respect of such offer is prepared in
-- src:38414 | accordance with section 243, and the profile statement is
-- src:38415 | prepared in accordance with section 246;
-- src:38417 | (b) a copy of the prospectus and a copy of the profile
-- src:38418 | statement, each of which has been signed in accordance
-- src:38419 | with subsection (4A), are lodged with the Authority, and
-- src:38420 | the prospectus is lodged no later than the profile statement;
-- src:38422 | (c) the prospectus and profile statement are registered by the
-- src:38423 | Authority;
-- src:38425 | (d) sufficient copies of the prospectus are made available for
-- src:38426 | collection at the times and places specified in the profile
-- src:38427 | statement; and
-- src:38429 | (e) the offer complies with such requirements as the Authority
-- src:38430 | may prescribe.
@ref s 240(4) (src:38408-38430)
GIVEN
    `the document is an extract from, or an abridged version of, a prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an extract from, or an abridged version of, a prospectus?
    `the prospectus is prepared in accordance with section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus prepared in accordance with section 243 (the contents section)?
    `the profile statement is prepared in accordance with section 246` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the profile statement prepared in accordance with section 246 (the contents section for profile statements)?
    `a copy of the prospectus and a copy of the profile statement, each signed in accordance with section 240(4A), are lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are a copy of the prospectus and a copy of the profile statement, each signed as section 240(4A) requires, lodged with the Authority?
    `the date the prospectus is lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the prospectus lodged with the Authority?
    `the date the profile statement is lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the profile statement lodged with the Authority?
    `the prospectus and profile statement are registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are both the prospectus and the profile statement registered by the Authority?
    `sufficient copies of the prospectus are made available for collection at the times and places specified in the profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are sufficient copies of the prospectus made available for collection at the times and places the profile statement specifies?
    `the offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer comply with the requirements the Authority has prescribed for the purpose of section 240(4)(e)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F5 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240(4) the offer may be made in or accompanied by a profile statement instead of a prospectus` MEANS
    IF `the document is an extract from, or an abridged version of, a prospectus` AND `the prospectus is prepared in accordance with section 243` AND `the profile statement is prepared in accordance with section 246` AND `a copy of the prospectus and a copy of the profile statement, each signed in accordance with section 240(4A), are lodged with the Authority` AND (`the date the prospectus is lodged` AT MOST `the date the profile statement is lodged`) AND `the prospectus and profile statement are registered by the Authority` AND `sufficient copies of the prospectus are made available for collection at the times and places specified in the profile statement` AND `the offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offer ... may be made in or accompanied by an extract from, or an abridged version of, a prospectus ... instead of a prospectus, if"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a permission; the other reading is JUST FALSE

-- s 240(4A): who must sign the copy lodged. One case for each person making the offer; the signing facts already take s 240(4B) and (4C) into account.
DECLARE `s 240(4A) who makes the offer` IS ONE OF
    `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is the issuer`
    `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is an individual and is not the issuer`
    `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is an entity, not being the government of a State, and is not the issuer`
    `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is the government of a State and is not the issuer`
    `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is none of these`

-- src:38434 | (4A) The copy of a prospectus or profile statement lodged with the
-- src:38435 | Authority must be signed —
-- src:38437 | (a) where the person making the offer is the issuer —
-- src:38439 | (i) in a case where the issuer is not the government of a
-- src:38440 | State — by every director or equivalent person of the
-- src:38441 | issuer and every person who is named therein as a
-- src:38446 | proposed director or an equivalent person of the
-- src:38447 | issuer; or
-- src:38449 | (ii) in a case where the issuer is the government of a
-- src:38450 | State — by an official of that government who is
-- src:38451 | authorised to sign the prospectus on its behalf;
-- src:38453 | (b) where the person making the offer is an individual and is
-- src:38454 | not the issuer —
-- src:38456 | (i) in a case where the issuer is not the government of a
-- src:38457 | State —
-- src:38459 | (A) by that person; and
-- src:38461 | (B) if the issuer is controlled by that person, one or
-- src:38462 | more of his or her related parties, or that person
-- src:38463 | and one or more of his or her related parties —
-- src:38464 | by every director or equivalent person of the
-- src:38465 | issuer and every person who is named therein
-- src:38466 | as a proposed director or an equivalent person
-- src:38467 | of the issuer; or
-- src:38469 | (ii) in a case where the issuer is the government of a
-- src:38470 | State — by that person;
-- src:38472 | (c) where the person making the offer is an entity (not being
-- src:38473 | the government of a State) and is not the issuer —
-- src:38475 | (i) in a case where the issuer is not the government of a
-- src:38476 | State —
-- src:38478 | (A) by every director or equivalent person of that
-- src:38479 | entity; and
-- src:38481 | (B) if the issuer is controlled by that entity, one or
-- src:38482 | more of its related parties, or that entity and
-- src:38483 | one or more of its related parties — by every
-- src:38484 | director or equivalent person of the issuer, and
-- src:38485 | every person who is named therein as a
-- src:38486 | proposed director or an equivalent person of
-- src:38487 | the issuer; or
-- src:38492 | (ii) in a case where the issuer is the government of a
-- src:38493 | State — by every director or equivalent person of
-- src:38494 | that entity; and
-- src:38496 | (d) where the person making the offer is the government of a
-- src:38497 | State and is not the issuer —
-- src:38499 | (i) in a case where the issuer is not the government of
-- src:38500 | another State —
-- src:38502 | (A) by an official of the government of the State
-- src:38503 | who is authorised to sign the prospectus on its
-- src:38504 | behalf; and
-- src:38506 | (B) if the issuer is controlled by that government,
-- src:38507 | one or more of its related parties, or that
-- src:38508 | government and one or more of its related
-- src:38509 | parties — by every director or every equivalent
-- src:38510 | person of the issuer, and every person who is
-- src:38511 | named therein as a proposed director or an
-- src:38512 | equivalent person of the issuer; or
-- src:38514 | (ii) in a case where the issuer is the government of
-- src:38515 | another State — by an official of the government of
-- src:38516 | the firstmentioned State who is authorised to sign the
-- src:38517 | prospectus on its behalf.
@ref s 240(4A) (src:38434-38517)
GIVEN
    `who makes the offer` IS A `s 240(4A) who makes the offer` @desc Who makes the offer: the issuer, an individual who is not the issuer, an entity (not the government of a State) that is not the issuer, the government of a State that is not the issuer, or none of these?
    `the issuer is the government of a State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issuer the government of a State (where the government of a State makes the offer: of another State)?
    `every director or equivalent person of the issuer and every person named in the document as a proposed director or equivalent person of the issuer has signed the copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has every director (or equivalent person) of the issuer, and every person the document names as a proposed director (or equivalent person) of the issuer, signed the copy (or had it signed for them by a person they authorised in writing)?
    `an official of the government that is the issuer, authorised to sign on its behalf, has signed the copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an official of the government that is the issuer, who is authorised to sign the prospectus on its behalf, signed the copy?
    `the individual who makes the offer has signed the copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the individual who makes the offer signed the copy?
    `every director or equivalent person of the entity that makes the offer has signed the copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has every director (or equivalent person) of the entity that makes the offer signed the copy (or had it signed for them by a person they authorised in writing)?
    `an official of the government that makes the offer, authorised to sign on its behalf, has signed the copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an official of the government that makes the offer, who is authorised to sign the prospectus on its behalf, signed the copy?
    `the issuer is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issuer controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of that person's related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(4A) the copy lodged with the Authority has been signed as required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who makes the offer`
    WHEN `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is the issuer` THEN
        IF `the issuer is the government of a State`
        THEN (IF `an official of the government that is the issuer, authorised to sign on its behalf, has signed the copy` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in a case where the issuer is the government of a State by an official of that government who is authorised to sign the prospectus on its behalf"
        ELSE (IF `every director or equivalent person of the issuer and every person named in the document as a proposed director or equivalent person of the issuer has signed the copy` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) in a case where the issuer is not the government of a State by every director or equivalent person of the issuer and every person who is named therein as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer"
    WHEN `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is an individual and is not the issuer` THEN
        IF `the issuer is the government of a State`
        THEN (IF `the individual who makes the offer has signed the copy` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in a case where the issuer is the government of a State by that person"
        ELSE (IF `the individual who makes the offer has signed the copy` AND ((NOT `the issuer is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties`) OR `every director or equivalent person of the issuer and every person named in the document as a proposed director or equivalent person of the issuer has signed the copy`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(A) by that person; and (B) if the issuer is controlled by that person, one or more of his or her related parties, or that person and one or more of his or her related parties by every director or equivalent person of the issuer and every person who is named therein as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer"
    WHEN `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is an entity, not being the government of a State, and is not the issuer` THEN
        IF `the issuer is the government of a State`
        THEN (IF `every director or equivalent person of the entity that makes the offer has signed the copy` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in a case where the issuer is the government of a State by every director or equivalent person of that entity"
        ELSE (IF `every director or equivalent person of the entity that makes the offer has signed the copy` AND ((NOT `the issuer is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties`) OR `every director or equivalent person of the issuer and every person named in the document as a proposed director or equivalent person of the issuer has signed the copy`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(A) by every director or equivalent person of that entity; and (B) if the issuer is controlled by that entity, one or more of its related parties, or that entity and one or more of its related parties by every director or equivalent person of the issuer, and every person who is named therein as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer"
    WHEN `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is the government of a State and is not the issuer` THEN
        IF `the issuer is the government of a State`
        THEN (IF `an official of the government that makes the offer, authorised to sign on its behalf, has signed the copy` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in a case where the issuer is the government of another State by an official of the government of the firstmentioned State who is authorised to sign the prospectus on its behalf"
        ELSE (IF `an official of the government that makes the offer, authorised to sign on its behalf, has signed the copy` AND ((NOT `the issuer is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties`) OR `every director or equivalent person of the issuer and every person named in the document as a proposed director or equivalent person of the issuer has signed the copy`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(A) by an official of the government of the State who is authorised to sign the prospectus on its behalf; and (B) if the issuer is controlled by that government, one or more of its related parties, or that government and one or more of its related parties by every director or every equivalent person of the issuer, and every person who is named therein as a proposed director or an equivalent person of the issuer"
    WHEN `s 240(4A) the person making the offer is none of these` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 240(4A) names four cases of the person making the offer and says nothing of any other

-- s 240(4B) and (4C): signature by a director (or proposed director), or by a person authorised in writing.
-- src:38519 | (4B) A requirement under subsection (4A) for the copy of a
-- src:38520 | prospectus or profile statement to be signed by a director or an
-- src:38521 | equivalent person is satisfied if the copy is signed —
-- src:38523 | (a) by that director or equivalent person; or
-- src:38525 | (b) by a person who is authorised in writing by that director or
-- src:38526 | equivalent person to sign on his or her behalf.
@ref s 240(4B) (src:38519-38526)
GIVEN
    `the copy is signed by that director or equivalent person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy signed by that director (or equivalent person)?
    `the copy is signed by a person authorised in writing by that director or equivalent person to sign on his or her behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy signed by a person whom that director (or equivalent person) has authorised in writing to sign on his or her behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(4B) the requirement for signature by a director or equivalent person is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the copy is signed by that director or equivalent person` OR `the copy is signed by a person authorised in writing by that director or equivalent person to sign on his or her behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is satisfied if the copy is signed (a) by that director or equivalent person; or (b) by a person who is authorised in writing by that director or equivalent person to sign on his or her behalf"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:38528 | (4C) A requirement under subsection (4A) for the copy of a
-- src:38529 | prospectus or profile statement to be signed by a person named
-- src:38530 | therein as a proposed director or an equivalent person is satisfied if
-- src:38531 | the copy is signed —
-- src:38533 | (a) by that proposed director or equivalent person; or
-- src:38535 | (b) by a person who is authorised in writing by that proposed
-- src:38536 | director or equivalent person to sign on his or her behalf.
@ref s 240(4C) (src:38528-38536)
GIVEN
    `the copy is signed by that proposed director or equivalent person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy signed by that person named in the document as a proposed director (or equivalent person)?
    `the copy is signed by a person authorised in writing by that proposed director or equivalent person to sign on his or her behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy signed by a person whom that proposed director (or equivalent person) has authorised in writing to sign on his or her behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(4C) the requirement for signature by a proposed director or equivalent person is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the copy is signed by that proposed director or equivalent person` OR `the copy is signed by a person authorised in writing by that proposed director or equivalent person to sign on his or her behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is satisfied if the copy is signed (a) by that proposed director or equivalent person; or (b) by a person who is authorised in writing by that proposed director or equivalent person to sign on his or her behalf"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- s 240(5): no offer in respect of an entity or business trust that has not been formed or does not exist.
DECLARE `s 240(5) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 240(5) make the offer`

-- src:38541 | (5) A person must not make any offer of securities or
-- src:38542 | securities‑based derivatives contracts in respect of an entity or a
-- src:38543 | business trust that has not been formed or does not exist.
@ref s 240(5) (src:38541-38543)
GIVEN
    `the person makes an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts (as section 239(6) says when a person makes an offer)?
    `the offer is in respect of an entity or a business trust that has not been formed or does not exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer in respect of an entity or business trust that has not been formed or does not exist?
    `this Subdivision applies to the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239A(1) and (2), s 239(8) and Subdivision (4): this Subdivision applies to the offer` answer for the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(5) the person must not make the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person makes an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`) OR (NOT `the offer is in respect of an entity or a business trust that has not been formed or does not exist`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not make any offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts in respect of an entity or a business trust that has not been formed or does not exist"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to an offer of securities"
        IF `this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer of the provision that may disapply this Subdivision was not worked out
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 240(5) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:38541-38543)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is the person who makes the offer?
    `what section 240(5) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240(5) the person must not make the offer` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 240(5) action`
`s 240(5) the person shall not make an offer in respect of an entity or business trust not formed` MEANS
    IF `what section 240(5) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 240(5) make the offer`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the offer was made in respect of an entity or business trust that has not been formed or does not exist; section 240(7) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 240(7): the offence of contravening (1) or (5), and its penalty.
-- src:38549 | (7) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) or (5) shall be
-- src:38550 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:38551 | exceeding $150,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:38552 | 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further
-- src:38553 | fine not exceeding $15,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:38554 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 240(7) (src:38549-38554)
GIVEN
    `what section 240(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240(1) the person must not make the offer` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 240(5) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240(5) the person must not make the offer` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F6 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240(7) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 240(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 240(5) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`what section 240(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 240(5) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1) or (5) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under subsection (1) or (5) was not worked out

@ref s 240(7) (the penalty) (src:38549-38554)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 240(7) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 150000, 24, TRUE, 15000  -- a fine not exceeding $150,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months), or both; a further fine not exceeding $15,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- s 240(8): when the Authority may register. A power with a closed "unless" gate and a period fixed in the text's words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (a)).
-- src:38556 | (8) The Authority may register a prospectus or a profile statement
-- src:38557 | on any day within the period prescribed by the Authority from the
-- src:38558 | date of lodgment thereof with the Authority, unless —
-- src:38560 | (a) the Authority gives to the person making the offer a notice
-- src:38561 | of an opportunity to be heard under subsection (15);
-- src:38563 | (b) the Authority gives to the person making the offer a notice
-- src:38564 | of an extension, in which case the Authority may, not later
-- src:38565 | than 28 days from the date of lodgment of the prospectus or
-- src:38566 | profile statement —
-- src:38568 | (i) register the prospectus or profile statement; or
-- src:38570 | (ii) give the person making the offer a notice of an
-- src:38571 | opportunity to be heard under subsection (15);
-- src:38573 | (c) the person making the offer applies in writing to extend the
-- src:38574 | period during which the prospectus or profile statement
-- src:38575 | may be registered, and the Authority grants an extension as
-- src:38576 | it thinks fit, in which case the Authority may, at any time up
-- src:38577 | to and including the date on which the extended period
-- src:38578 | ends —
-- src:38580 | (i) register the prospectus or profile statement; or
-- src:38582 | (ii) give the person making the offer a notice of an
-- src:38583 | opportunity to be heard under subsection (15); or
-- src:38585 | (d) the person making the offer gives a written notice to the
-- src:38586 | Authority to withdraw the lodgment of the prospectus or
-- src:38591 | profile statement, in which case the Authority must not
-- src:38592 | register the prospectus or profile statement.
@ref s 240(8) (src:38556-38592)
GIVEN
    `the date of lodgment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus or profile statement lodged with the Authority?
    `the day on which registration is asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the Authority register the prospectus or profile statement?
    `the number of days from lodgment within which the Authority has prescribed that it may register` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days from the date of lodgment has the Authority prescribed for registering a prospectus or profile statement?
    `the Authority gives the person making the offer a notice of an opportunity to be heard under subsection (15)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority given the person making the offer a notice of an opportunity to be heard under section 240(15)?
    `the Authority gives the person making the offer a notice of an extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority given the person making the offer a notice of an extension?
    `the person making the offer applies in writing to extend the period and the Authority grants an extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer applied in writing to extend the period during which the prospectus or profile statement may be registered, and has the Authority granted an extension?
    `the date on which the extended period ends` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the extended period end (any date if no extension was granted)?
    `the person making the offer gives a written notice to the Authority to withdraw the lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer given the Authority a written notice withdrawing the lodgment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F9 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240(8) the Authority may register the prospectus or profile statement on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person making the offer gives a written notice to the Authority to withdraw the lodgment`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in which case the Authority must not register the prospectus or profile statement"
        IF `the Authority gives the person making the offer a notice of an opportunity to be heard under subsection (15)`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless (a) the Authority gives to the person making the offer a notice of an opportunity to be heard under subsection (15)"
        IF `the Authority gives the person making the offer a notice of an extension`
        THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of lodgment` `the day on which registration is asked about` 28 Days THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Authority may, not later than 28 days from the date of lodgment of the prospectus or profile statement"
        IF `the person making the offer applies in writing to extend the period and the Authority grants an extension`
        THEN (IF `the day on which registration is asked about` AT MOST `the date on which the extended period ends` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Authority may, at any time up to and including the date on which the extended period ends"
        OTHERWISE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of lodgment` `the day on which registration is asked about` `the number of days from lodgment within which the Authority has prescribed that it may register` Days THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on any day within the period prescribed by the Authority from the date of lodgment thereof with the Authority"

-- s 240(8A): after a hearing notice, the Authority may proceed with registration on a date it considers appropriate, but not earlier than the prescribed day. A "Where" gate: JUST FALSE under rule (b) of the periods ruling (fork F7).
-- src:38596 | (8A) Where, after a notice of an opportunity to be heard has been
-- src:38597 | given under subsection (8)(a), (b)(ii) or (c)(ii), the Authority decides
-- src:38598 | not to refuse registration of the prospectus or profile statement, the
-- src:38599 | Authority may proceed with the registration on such date as it
-- src:38600 | considers appropriate, except that that date must not be earlier than
-- src:38601 | such day from the date of lodgment of the prospectus or profile
-- src:38602 | statement with the Authority as the Authority may prescribe.
@ref s 240(8A) (src:38596-38602)
GIVEN
    `the Authority gave a notice of an opportunity to be heard under subsection (8)(a), (b)(ii) or (c)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority given a notice of an opportunity to be heard under section 240(8)(a), (b)(ii) or (c)(ii)?
    `the Authority decides not to refuse registration of the prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority decided not to refuse registration of the prospectus or profile statement?
    `the date of lodgment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus or profile statement lodged with the Authority?
    `the date on which the Authority proceeds with the registration` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the Authority proceed with the registration?
    `the number of days from lodgment before which the Authority has prescribed that it must not register` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days from the date of lodgment has the Authority prescribed as the earliest day for proceeding with registration under section 240(8A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F7 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240(8A) the Authority may proceed with the registration on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Authority gave a notice of an opportunity to be heard under subsection (8)(a), (b)(ii) or (c)(ii)`) OR (NOT `the Authority decides not to refuse registration of the prospectus or profile statement`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, after a notice of an opportunity to be heard has been given under subsection (8)(a), (b)(ii) or (c)(ii), the Authority decides not to refuse registration of the prospectus or profile statement, the Authority may proceed with the registration"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
        IF `the date on which the Authority proceeds with the registration` LESS THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of lodgment` `the number of days from lodgment before which the Authority has prescribed that it must not register` Days)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that that date must not be earlier than such day from the date of lodgment of the prospectus or profile statement with the Authority as the Authority may prescribe"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 240(9): a preliminary document is not registered until the full prospectus is lodged.
-- src:38612 | (9) Where a prospectus lodged with the Authority is a preliminary
-- src:38613 | document, the Authority must not register the prospectus unless a
-- src:38614 | copy of the prospectus which has been signed in accordance with
-- src:38615 | subsection (4A) and which contains the information required to be
-- src:38616 | stipulated in the prospectus under section 243, including such
-- src:38617 | information which could be omitted from the preliminary
-- src:38618 | document by virtue of subsection (3), has been lodged with the
-- src:38619 | Authority.
@ref s 240(9) (src:38612-38619)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus lodged with the Authority is a preliminary document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus lodged with the Authority a preliminary document?
    `a copy of the prospectus signed in accordance with section 240(4A) and containing the information required to be stipulated under section 243, including the information that could be left out of a preliminary document, has been lodged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the prospectus been lodged that is signed as section 240(4A) requires and contains all the information section 243 requires (including what a preliminary document may leave out)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(9) the Authority must not register the prospectus` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the prospectus lodged with the Authority is a preliminary document`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a prospectus lodged with the Authority is a preliminary document"
        IF `a copy of the prospectus signed in accordance with section 240(4A) and containing the information required to be stipulated under section 243, including the information that could be left out of a preliminary document, has been lodged`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Authority must not register the prospectus unless a copy of the prospectus which has been signed in accordance with subsection (4A) and which contains the information required to be stipulated in the prospectus under section 243"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 240(9A): an amendment may be lodged before, but not after, registration.
-- src:38621 | (9A) A person making an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:38622 | derivatives contracts may lodge any amendment to a prospectus or
-- src:38623 | profile statement in respect of that offer at any time before, but not
-- src:38624 | after, the registration of the prospectus or profile statement by the
-- src:38625 | Authority.
@ref s 240(9A) (src:38621-38625)
GIVEN
    `the day on which the amendment would be lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the amendment be lodged?
    `the day the Authority registered the prospectus or profile statement` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the Authority register the prospectus or profile statement? (NOTHING if it has not yet registered it.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(9A) the person may lodge an amendment on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the Authority registered the prospectus or profile statement`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST registered THEN
        IF `the day on which the amendment would be lodged` LESS THAN registered
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before, but not after, the registration of the prospectus or profile statement by the Authority"

-- s 240(10) and (11): the date an amended prospectus or profile statement is taken to have been lodged, for the purposes of subsection (8).
-- src:38629 | (10) Subject to subsection (11) —
-- src:38631 | (a) where any amendment to a prospectus is lodged, the
-- src:38632 | prospectus and any profile statement which is lodged is
-- src:38633 | deemed for the purposes of subsection (8) to have been
-- src:38634 | lodged when such amendment was lodged; and
-- src:38636 | (b) where any amendment to a profile statement is lodged, the
-- src:38637 | profile statement is deemed for the purposes of
-- src:38642 | subsection (8) to have been lodged when such amendment
-- src:38643 | was lodged.
-- src:38645 | (11) Where an amendment to a prospectus or profile statement is
-- src:38646 | lodged with the consent of the Authority, the prospectus or profile
-- src:38647 | statement as amended is deemed, for the purposes of subsection (8),
-- src:38648 | to have been lodged when the original prospectus or profile statement
-- src:38649 | was lodged with the Authority.
@ref s 240(10) and (11) (src:38629-38649)
GIVEN
    `the date the original was lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the original prospectus or profile statement lodged with the Authority?
    `an amendment is lodged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an amendment to the prospectus or profile statement been lodged?
    `the date the amendment is lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the amendment lodged (any date if none)?
    `the amendment is lodged with the consent of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amendment lodged with the consent of the Authority?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 240(10) and (11) the date taken as the date of lodgment for the purposes of subsection (8)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an amendment is lodged` AND `the amendment is lodged with the consent of the Authority`
        THEN `the date the original was lodged`  -- (11): "the prospectus or profile statement as amended is deemed, for the purposes of subsection (8), to have been lodged when the original prospectus or profile statement was lodged with the Authority"
        IF `an amendment is lodged`
        THEN `the date the amendment is lodged`  -- (10): "deemed for the purposes of subsection (8) to have been lodged when such amendment was lodged"
        OTHERWISE `the date the original was lodged`  -- no amendment: subsection (8) counts from "the date of lodgment", read as the day it was lodged

-- s 240(11A): an amendment is part of the original.
-- src:38651 | (11A) An amendment to a prospectus or profile statement that is
-- src:38652 | lodged is treated as part of the original prospectus or profile
-- src:38653 | statement.
@ref s 240(11A) (src:38651-38653)
GIVEN
    `an amendment to the prospectus or profile statement is lodged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an amendment to the prospectus or profile statement lodged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(11A) the amendment is treated as part of the original prospectus or profile statement` MEANS
    IF `an amendment to the prospectus or profile statement is lodged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of an amendment that is lodged

-- s 240(12): the Authority may publish, and the person must provide a copy in the form or medium required.
DECLARE `s 240(12) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 240(12) provide the Authority with a copy in the form or medium required`

-- src:38655 | (12) The Authority may, for public information, publish —
-- src:38657 | (a) a prospectus or profile statement lodged with the Authority
-- src:38658 | under this section; and
-- src:38660 | (b) where applicable, the translation thereof in the English
-- src:38661 | language lodged with the Authority under section 318A(1),
-- src:38663 | and, for the purposes of this subsection, the person making the offer
-- src:38664 | must provide the Authority with a copy of the prospectus or profile
-- src:38665 | statement and, where applicable, the translation in such form or
-- src:38666 | medium for publication as the Authority may require.
@ref s 240(12) (src:38655-38666)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus or profile statement is lodged with the Authority under section 240` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus or profile statement lodged with the Authority under section 240?
    `the Authority requires a form or medium for the publication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority require a particular form or medium for publication of the prospectus or profile statement (and any English translation)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(12) the person making the offer must provide the Authority with a copy in the form or medium required` MEANS
    IF `the prospectus or profile statement is lodged with the Authority under section 240` AND `the Authority requires a form or medium for the publication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for a prospectus or profile statement lodged "under this section" and for "such form or medium for publication as the Authority may require"

@ref s 240(12) (the duty as a rule) (src:38655-38666)
GIVEN
    `the person making the offer` IS A Party @desc Who makes the offer?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 240(12) action`
`s 240(12) the person making the offer must provide the Authority with a copy for publication` MEANS
    PARTY `the person making the offer`
    MUST `s 240(12) provide the Authority with a copy in the form or medium required`

-- s 240(13): the Authority must refuse to register a prospectus on any of the grounds.
-- src:38668 | (13) The Authority must refuse to register a prospectus if —
-- src:38670 | (a) the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus contains
-- src:38671 | a false or misleading statement;
-- src:38673 | (b) there is an omission from the prospectus of any
-- src:38674 | information that is required to be included in it under
-- src:38675 | section 243;
-- src:38677 | (c) the copy of the prospectus that is lodged with the Authority
-- src:38678 | is not signed in accordance with subsection (4A);
-- src:38680 | (d) the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus does not
-- src:38681 | comply with the requirements of this Act;
-- src:38683 | (e) any written consent of an expert to the issue of the
-- src:38684 | prospectus required under section 249, or a copy thereof
-- src:38685 | which is verified as prescribed, is not lodged with the
-- src:38686 | Authority;
-- src:38691 | (ea) any written consent of an issue manager to the issue of the
-- src:38692 | prospectus required under section 249A(1), or a copy
-- src:38693 | thereof which is verified as prescribed, is not lodged with
-- src:38694 | the Authority;
-- src:38696 | (eb) any written consent of an underwriter to the issue of the
-- src:38697 | prospectus required under section 249A(2), or a copy
-- src:38698 | thereof which is verified as prescribed, is not lodged with
-- src:38699 | the Authority; or
-- src:38701 | (f) the Authority is of the opinion that it is not in the public
-- src:38702 | interest to do so.
@ref s 240(13) (src:38668-38702)
GIVEN
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus contains a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that the prospectus contains a false or misleading statement?
    `information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243 is omitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission from the prospectus of any information that section 243 requires to be included in it?
    `the copy of the prospectus lodged with the Authority is not signed in accordance with section 240(4A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy of the prospectus lodged with the Authority not signed as section 240(4A) requires?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus does not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that the prospectus does not comply with the requirements of this Act?
    `a written consent of an expert required under section 249 (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a written consent of an expert to the issue of the prospectus, required under section 249 (or a copy verified as prescribed), not lodged with the Authority?
    `a written consent of an issue manager required under section 249A(1) (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a written consent of an issue manager to the issue of the prospectus, required under section 249A(1) (or a copy verified as prescribed), not lodged with the Authority?
    `a written consent of an underwriter required under section 249A(2) (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a written consent of an underwriter to the issue of the prospectus, required under section 249A(2) (or a copy verified as prescribed), not lodged with the Authority?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that it is not in the public interest to register the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that it is not in the public interest to register the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(13) the Authority must refuse to register the prospectus` MEANS
    IF `the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus contains a false or misleading statement` OR `information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243 is omitted` OR `the copy of the prospectus lodged with the Authority is not signed in accordance with section 240(4A)` OR `the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus does not comply with the requirements of this Act` OR `a written consent of an expert required under section 249 (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` OR `a written consent of an issue manager required under section 249A(1) (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` OR `a written consent of an underwriter required under section 249A(2) (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` OR `the Authority is of the opinion that it is not in the public interest to register the prospectus`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Authority must refuse to register a prospectus if"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- s 240(14): the same for a profile statement.
-- src:38704 | (14) The Authority must refuse to register a profile statement if —
-- src:38706 | (a) the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement
-- src:38707 | contains a false or misleading statement;
-- src:38709 | (b) there is an omission from the profile statement of
-- src:38710 | information required by section 246 to be included in it
-- src:38711 | or an inclusion in the profile statement of information
-- src:38712 | prohibited by that section from being included in it;
-- src:38714 | (c) the copy of the profile statement that is lodged with the
-- src:38715 | Authority is not signed in accordance with
-- src:38716 | subsection (4A);
-- src:38718 | (ca) any written consent of an expert to the issue of the profile
-- src:38719 | statement required under section 249, or a copy thereof
-- src:38720 | which is verified as prescribed, is not lodged with the
-- src:38721 | Authority;
-- src:38723 | (cb) any written consent of an issue manager to the issue of the
-- src:38724 | profile statement required under section 249A(1), or a copy
-- src:38725 | thereof which is verified as prescribed, is not lodged with
-- src:38726 | the Authority;
-- src:38728 | (cc) any written consent of an underwriter to the issue of the
-- src:38729 | profile statement required under section 249A(2), or a copy
-- src:38730 | thereof which is verified as prescribed, is not lodged with
-- src:38731 | the Authority;
-- src:38733 | (d) the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement
-- src:38734 | does not comply with the requirements of this Act;
-- src:38739 | (e) the prospectus has not been registered by the Authority; or
-- src:38741 | (f) the Authority is of the opinion that it is not in the public
-- src:38742 | interest to do so.
@ref s 240(14) (src:38704-38742)
GIVEN
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement contains a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that the profile statement contains a false or misleading statement?
    `information required by section 246 is omitted from the profile statement, or information section 246 prohibits is included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is information that section 246 requires omitted from the profile statement, or information that section 246 prohibits included in it?
    `the copy of the profile statement lodged with the Authority is not signed in accordance with section 240(4A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy of the profile statement lodged with the Authority not signed as section 240(4A) requires?
    `a written consent of an expert required under section 249 (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a written consent of an expert to the issue of the profile statement, required under section 249 (or a copy verified as prescribed), not lodged with the Authority?
    `a written consent of an issue manager required under section 249A(1) (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a written consent of an issue manager to the issue of the profile statement, required under section 249A(1) (or a copy verified as prescribed), not lodged with the Authority?
    `a written consent of an underwriter required under section 249A(2) (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a written consent of an underwriter to the issue of the profile statement, required under section 249A(2) (or a copy verified as prescribed), not lodged with the Authority?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement does not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that the profile statement does not comply with the requirements of this Act?
    `the prospectus has not been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prospectus not been registered by the Authority?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that it is not in the public interest to register the profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that it is not in the public interest to register the profile statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(14) the Authority must refuse to register the profile statement` MEANS
    IF `the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement contains a false or misleading statement` OR `information required by section 246 is omitted from the profile statement, or information section 246 prohibits is included` OR `the copy of the profile statement lodged with the Authority is not signed in accordance with section 240(4A)` OR `a written consent of an expert required under section 249 (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` OR `a written consent of an issue manager required under section 249A(1) (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` OR `a written consent of an underwriter required under section 249A(2) (or a verified copy) is not lodged with the Authority` OR `the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement does not comply with the requirements of this Act` OR `the prospectus has not been registered by the Authority` OR `the Authority is of the opinion that it is not in the public interest to register the profile statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Authority must refuse to register a profile statement if"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- s 240(15): the opportunity to be heard before a refusal, and its exception.
-- src:38744 | (15) The Authority must not refuse to register a prospectus under
-- src:38745 | subsection (13) or a profile statement under subsection (14) without
-- src:38746 | giving the person making the offer an opportunity to be heard, except
-- src:38747 | that an opportunity to be heard need not be given if the refusal is on
-- src:38748 | the ground that it is not in the public interest to register the prospectus
-- src:38749 | or profile statement on the basis of any of the following
-- src:38750 | circumstances:
-- src:38752 | (a) the person making the offer (being an entity), the issuer or
-- src:38753 | the trustee‑manager of the business trust or, where
-- src:38754 | applicable, the underlying entity or the business trust is
-- src:38755 | in the course of being wound up or otherwise dissolved,
-- src:38756 | whether in Singapore or elsewhere;
-- src:38758 | (b) the person making the offer (being an individual) is an
-- src:38759 | undischarged bankrupt, whether in Singapore or
-- src:38760 | elsewhere;
-- src:38762 | (c) a receiver, a receiver and manager or an equivalent person
-- src:38763 | has been appointed, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, in
-- src:38764 | relation to or in respect of any property of the person
-- src:38765 | making the offer (being an entity), the issuer or the
-- src:38766 | trustee‑manager of the business trust or, where applicable,
-- src:38767 | the underlying entity, or in relation to or in respect of the
-- src:38768 | trust property of the business trust.
@ref s 240(15) (src:38744-38768)
GIVEN
    `the Authority refuses to register a prospectus under subsection (13) or a profile statement under subsection (14)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority refuse to register a prospectus under section 240(13) or a profile statement under section 240(14)?
    `the refusal is on the ground that it is not in the public interest to register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the refusal on the ground that it is not in the public interest to register the prospectus or profile statement?
    `the entity making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or, where applicable, the underlying entity or the business trust is in the course of being wound up or otherwise dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the offer (an entity), the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or (where applicable) the underlying entity or the business trust in the course of being wound up or otherwise dissolved, in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the individual making the offer is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the individual making the offer an undischarged bankrupt, in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `a receiver, receiver and manager or equivalent person has been appointed over the property of the entity making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager or the underlying entity, or over the trust property of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a receiver, receiver and manager or equivalent person been appointed, in Singapore or elsewhere, over any property of the entity making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or (where applicable) the underlying entity, or over the trust property of the business trust?
    `the refusal is made on the basis of one of those circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the refusal made on the basis of one of those three circumstances (winding up or dissolution, undischarged bankruptcy, appointment of a receiver)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(15) the Authority must give the person making the offer an opportunity to be heard before refusing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Authority refuses to register a prospectus under subsection (13) or a profile statement under subsection (14)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for a refusal "under subsection (13) or a profile statement under subsection (14)"
        IF `the refusal is on the ground that it is not in the public interest to register` AND `the refusal is made on the basis of one of those circumstances` AND (`the entity making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or, where applicable, the underlying entity or the business trust is in the course of being wound up or otherwise dissolved` OR `the individual making the offer is an undischarged bankrupt` OR `a receiver, receiver and manager or equivalent person has been appointed over the property of the entity making the offer, the issuer, the trustee-manager or the underlying entity, or over the trust property of the business trust`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that an opportunity to be heard need not be given if the refusal is on the ground that it is not in the public interest to register the prospectus or profile statement on the basis of any of the following circumstances"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 240(16): appeal to the Minister within 30 days after notification; the Minister's decision is final.
-- src:38772 | (16) Any person making an offer may, within 30 days after the
-- src:38773 | person is notified that the Authority has refused to register a
-- src:38774 | prospectus or profile statement to which the person’s offer relates
-- src:38775 | under subsection (13) or (14), appeal to the Minister, whose decision
-- src:38776 | is final.
@ref s 240(16) (src:38772-38776)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has refused to register the prospectus or profile statement under subsection (13) or (14)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority refused to register the prospectus or profile statement to which the person's offer relates under section 240(13) or (14)?
    `the date the person is notified of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the person notified that the Authority refused to register?
    `the date the person appeals to the Minister` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the person appeal to the Minister?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F9 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240(16) the person making an offer may appeal to the Minister` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Authority has refused to register the prospectus or profile statement under subsection (13) or (14)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the appeal is given "within 30 days after the person is notified that the Authority has refused to register"
        IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the person is notified of the refusal` `the date the person appeals to the Minister` 30 Days
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after the person is notified that the Authority has refused to register a prospectus or profile statement"

@ref s 240(16) (the Minister's decision is final) (src:38772-38776)
GIVEN
    `the person has appealed to the Minister under subsection (16)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person appealed to the Minister under section 240(16)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(16) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` MEANS
    IF `the person has appealed to the Minister under subsection (16)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whose decision is final" speaks only of the Minister's decision on an appeal under the subsection

-- s 240(17): the offence of issuing a prospectus, or accepting applications or allotting, before registration.
DECLARE `s 240(17) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 240(17) issue, circulate or distribute the prospectus or profile statement before registration`
    `s 240(17) accept an application, or allot, issue or sell, before registration`

-- src:38778 | (17) If —
-- src:38780 | (a) a prospectus or profile statement is issued, circulated or
-- src:38781 | distributed before it has been registered by the Authority;
-- src:38782 | or
-- src:38787 | (b) an application to subscribe for or purchase securities or
-- src:38788 | securities‑based derivatives contracts is accepted, or
-- src:38789 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts are
-- src:38790 | allotted, issued or sold, before a prospectus and, where
-- src:38791 | applicable, profile statement in respect of the securities or
-- src:38792 | securities‑based derivatives contracts has been registered
-- src:38793 | by the Authority,
-- src:38795 | the person making the offer and every person who is knowingly a
-- src:38796 | party to —
-- src:38798 | (c) the issue, circulation or distribution of the prospectus or
-- src:38799 | profile statement;
-- src:38801 | (d) the acceptance of the application to subscribe for or
-- src:38802 | purchase the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:38803 | contracts; or
-- src:38805 | (e) the allotment, issue or sale of the securities or
-- src:38806 | securities‑based derivatives contracts,
-- src:38808 | as the case may be, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:38809 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $150,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:38810 | term not exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:38811 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $15,000 for every day or part
-- src:38812 | of a day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 240(17) (src:38778-38812)
GIVEN
    `this Subdivision applies to the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239A(1) and (2), s 239(8) and Subdivision (4): this Subdivision applies to the offer` answer for the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `a prospectus or profile statement is issued, circulated or distributed before it has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a prospectus or profile statement issued, circulated or distributed before the Authority has registered it?
    `an application is accepted, or securities or securities-based derivatives contracts are allotted, issued or sold, before the prospectus and (where applicable) the profile statement have been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an application to subscribe for or purchase accepted, or are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts allotted, issued or sold, before the prospectus and (where applicable) the profile statement have been registered by the Authority?
    `the person is the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the person making the offer?
    `the person is knowingly a party to the issue, circulation or distribution, to the acceptance of the application, or to the allotment, issue or sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person knowingly a party to the issue, circulation or distribution of the prospectus or profile statement, to the acceptance of the application, or to the allotment, issue or sale?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F8 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240(17) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to an offer of securities"
        IF (NOT `a prospectus or profile statement is issued, circulated or distributed before it has been registered by the Authority`) AND (NOT `an application is accepted, or securities or securities-based derivatives contracts are allotted, issued or sold, before the prospectus and (where applicable) the profile statement have been registered by the Authority`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If (a) a prospectus or profile statement is issued, circulated or distributed before it has been registered by the Authority; or (b) an application to subscribe for or purchase securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is accepted"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        IF `this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer of the provision that may disapply this Subdivision was not worked out
        IF `the person is the person making the offer` OR `the person is knowingly a party to the issue, circulation or distribution, to the acceptance of the application, or to the allotment, issue or sale`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person making the offer and every person who is knowingly a party to" names the persons liable and says nothing of anyone else  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 240(17) (the penalty) (src:38778-38812)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 240(17) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 150000, 24, TRUE, 15000  -- a fine not exceeding $150,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months), or both; a further fine not exceeding $15,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

@ref s 240(17) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:38778-38812)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is the person?
    `what section 240(17) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240(17) the person is guilty of an offence` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 240(17) action`
`s 240(17) the person shall not accept an application or allot before registration` MEANS
    IF `what section 240(17) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 240(17) accept an application, or allot, issue or sell, before registration`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "an application was accepted, or securities were allotted, issued or sold, before registration; section 240(17) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 240(18): this section is subject to section 240A.
-- src:38816 | (18) This section is subject to section 240A.
@ref s 240(18) (src:38816-38816)
GIVEN
    `the offer is part of a debenture issuance programme to which section 240A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme (so that section 240A applies)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(18) this section yields to section 240A for the offer` MEANS
    IF `the offer is part of a debenture issuance programme to which section 240A applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says this section is subject to section 240A and says nothing of an offer outside it

-- s 240(19): a "statement" includes any information presented, in text or otherwise.
-- src:38818 | (19) For the purposes of subsections (13)(a) and (14)(a), any
-- src:38819 | reference to a statement includes a reference to any information
-- src:38820 | presented, regardless of whether such information is in text or
-- src:38821 | otherwise.
@ref s 240(19) (src:38818-38821)
GIVEN
    `the information is presented in or with the prospectus or profile statement, whether in text or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information presented in or with the prospectus or profile statement, whether in text or in some other form?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(19) the information is a statement for the purposes of subsections (13)(a) and (14)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the information is presented in or with the prospectus or profile statement, whether in text or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to a statement includes a reference to any information presented, regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise" lists without closing the list
